                'answer_type' => 'text',
                'correct_answer' => '120',
                'explanation' => 'The orbital radius is r = 6400 + 3600 = 10000 km = 10⁷ m. The orbital period is T = 2π√(r³/GM), where GM = gr² = 9.8 × (6.4 × 10⁶)² = 9.8 × 4.096 × 10¹³ = 4.01408 × 10¹⁴. So T = 2π√((10⁷)³/(4.01408 × 10¹⁴)) = 2π√(10²¹/(4.01408 × 10¹⁴)) = 2π√(2.49 × 10⁶) = 2π × 1577.97 = 9917.8 seconds ≈ 120 minutes.',
